# Rebuild plugin dist for the running UI

Web and desktop resolve first-party plugins through public `dist` exports
(`svelte-package` / `prepack`). Storybook may alias source; the running app
does not.

After changing `@lapis-notes/ai` or another dist-exporting plugin, rebuild
that package before validating the UI:

```bash
pnpm --filter @lapis-notes/ai build
```

Use the owning package name for other plugins (`@lapis-notes/markdown`,
`@lapis-notes/search`, `@lapis-notes/file-explorer`, and so on). Then restart
the long-running web Vite or desktop process when hot reload still shows the
old surface. Do not treat package tests or Storybook plays as proof that
`dist` was refreshed.
